{# Two facts, and this article was written knowing only one of them.

   The one it knew: there are no accounts here. A booking is found by session
   id -- see BookingRepository::forSession() -- so the list is the browser's,
   and the reference is the only part of a booking somebody carries away.

   The one it did not: no email is sent, ever. There is no mailer in this
   project. This article had a section telling the reader their ticket "goes to
   the address you gave at checkout" and to look in their spam folder if it had
   not turned up -- advice for waiting on something that was never coming,
   picked up in good faith from the confirmation page, which said the same
   thing and no longer does.

   So the honest answer to "my ticket did not arrive" is that none is sent, and
   the rest of the article is where the booking actually is. #}
<h2>No ticket is emailed</h2>
<p>
    Nothing arrives in your inbox, however long you wait, and there is no
    spam folder worth checking. {{ config('app.name') }} is a demonstration:
    it takes a booking, gives it a reference and keeps it, and it issues no
    ticket and contacts no airline.
</p>

<h2>The reference is the booking</h2>
<p>
    If you saw a booking reference on the confirmation page, the booking
    exists. Write it down: it is the one part of a booking you carry away from
    the browser you made it in.
</p>

<h2>It is on this site too &mdash; in this browser</h2>
<p>
    Every booking you make appears under <a href="/my/bookings">My
    bookings</a>. There are no accounts here, so that list belongs to the
    browser you booked in. Open it on another device, or after clearing your
    browsing data, and it will be empty.
</p>
<p>
    Nothing is lost when that happens and the booking still stands. But the
    reference is the part of it you keep, which is the whole reason to write it
    down.
</p>

<h2>The address you gave</h2>
<p>
    It is stored with the booking and shown on its own page, under
    <a href="/my/bookings">My bookings</a>, so you can see what was typed. Since
    nothing is sent to it, a typo there costs you nothing.
</p>
